        "client_msg_id": "a4b21114-837a-44ab-b58e-07105a6213f0",
        "text": "Hey <@U05HDNRKR7X> :blush:\nHow are you?\nI recently started the Matt Palmer's Mage course with AWS.\n\nI created my redshift database and my S3 bucket.\nI did try to authenticate Mage with AWS but\nI got the error connection refused ;\n`ConnectionRefusedError: [Errno 111] Connection refused`\n`InterfaceError: ('communication error', ConnectionRefusedError(111, 'Connection refused'))`\nI've been Stuck with that for 3 days...\nI have no clue what the issue is, I guess the network infrastructure (VPC, Security Group, ... ) but I have no idea what I did wrong.\n\nHere is my AWS *Network Setup*:\n• 1 VPC with 3 public and 3 private subnets\n• Route tables, 1 internet gateway, and 3 NAT gateways\n• redshift clusters\n• ec2 instances\nThe redshift cluster are in the private subnets and the ec2 instances are in the public ones.\n\nYour input\/advice will be a benediction!\nThank you\n<#C04J4U9NK46|de-course-aws>",
